{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"printf '\\\\n--- method qualifications ---\\\\n'; sed -n '70,190p' global_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/METHOD.md; printf '\\\\n--- source declarations ---\\\\n'; rg -n '\"'^def |''^class |knots|ridge|rho|Wald|Clopper|GCV|safety|synthetic|dataset|galax|forest|census'\"' global_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src; printf '\\\\n--- final comparisons ---\\\\n'; jq '.final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[0].solution.case_summaries | map({case,comparisons:(.comparisons|map_values({width_difference:.difference,ratio:.ratio,baseline_coverage:.baseline_coverage.coverage,valid_gain_supported,valid_loss_supported,inconclusive_or_invalid,zero_width_count}))})' paper_data.json; printf '\\\\n--- local task names ---\\\\n'; ls -la task; printf '\\\\n--- provenance presence ---\\\\n'; for path in references.bib references_provenance.json; do if [ -f \\\"\"'$path\" ]; then ls -l \"$path\"; else printf '\"'%s absent\\\\n' \\\"\"'$path\"; fi; done'","aggregated_output":"\n--- method qualifications ---\nOnly the known outcome support [0,1] is used to clip the resulting interval.\nAn empty numerical intersection is conservatively replaced by [0,1]. This\nargument does not assume unconditional independence of cross-fitted folds.\nThe safety interval can be much wider than Wald or Clopper-Pearson.\n\n## Oracle frontier and asymptotic qualifications\n\nFor fixed g, write m(S)=E[Y|S], rho=N/(n+N). Then\n\n    Var(mu_hat_g) = Var(Y-rho*g(S))/n + rho^2*Var(g(S))/N\n    Var(mu_hat_m) = E[Var(Y|S)]/n + Var(m(S))/(n+N).\n\nThe excess variance relative to m is rho/n times Var(g(S)-m(S)); additive\nconstants in g cancel. The reduction over the best unrestricted affine score\ncontrol is N/[n(n+N)] times E[(m-Pi_affine(m))^2]. For constant scores the affine\nprojection is the intercept. `study.py:oracle_frontier` implements this formula\nfrom supplied analytic moments, not hidden evaluation targets.\n\nFor the Wald approximation, require n,N tending to infinity with a positive\nfinite limiting ratio, a nondegenerate limiting variance, and fold calibrators\nconverging in L2 to the same deterministic bounded function. Conditional\ncentering and cross-fitting then make nuisance empirical-mean errors negligible\nrelative to n^(-1/2). This is not an assertion of finite-fold independence.\nThe fixed spline dictionary need not consistently estimate arbitrary m, so\nattainment of the oracle frontier is not claimed. Nonlinear information,\nenough training labels, and stable nuisance estimation are needed for gains.\nAffine m, uninformative scores, small N, rare events, and nuisance estimation\ncosts are important no-gain or failure regimes. Distribution shift is excluded.\n\n## Evidence and unfinished work\n\nOnly permitted static candidate/interface inspection and editing occurred.\nNo candidate code was executed or imported; no tests, benchmarks, searches,\npackage installs, data downloads, or evaluations were run. No prohibited\nliterature was encountered. No literature outside the provided task text was\nread. No empirically measured coverage, gain, timing, or score is reported.\nThe fold isolation above is a source-level design audit, not an executed test.\n\n`study.py` supplies unexecuted paired uncertainty and per-repetition record\nhelpers: exact binomial coverage intervals, paired t intervals for mean width\ndifferences, and explicit validity-track labels. They are not a completed\nexperiment runner. Paired repetitions, independent synthetic truth checks,\nreal-data masking studies, established-baseline comparisons, executable audit\ntests, and the conference paper/PDF remain uncompleted because this stage\nallows candidate preparation only and explicitly forbids their execution or\nexternal source access. The harness alone performs the official evaluation.\n\n--- source declarations ---\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/study.py:14:def oracle_frontier(labeled_count, unlabeled_count, conditional_noise_variance,\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/study.py:30:def paired_uncertainty(covered, candidate_widths, baseline_widths):\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/study.py:59:def repetition_record(repetition, method, estimate, lower, upper, validity_track):\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:36:All knots and tuning use complementary labeled folds only. Unlabeled scores\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:37:are split too; the pooling coefficient is N/(n+N). The RPC returns a stabilized Wald\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:40:never used to select a narrower interval. Wald coverage is only asymptotic;\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:52:class ScoreCalibrator:\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:53:    \"\"\"Small ridge linear-spline family, tuned exclusively on its fit sample.\"\"\"\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:62:        self.knots = np.empty(0)\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:76:        for knots in knot_families:\nglobal_memory/ideas/02_honest_nonlinear_score_controls_with_a_finite_sample_safety_track/program_1/src/program.py:77: 